WEBVTT

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:47.050
<b>Speaking of Crossovers,
 Don't Forget About Alien vs. Predator</b>

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.920
Hey, listen up, guys.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.560
We have a special treat this week

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.760
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan</b>

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.760
to commemorate the 26th 
episode of the new season.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.770
A special treat?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.350
Wait, 26 is kind of a random number.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:59.400
Basically, we were told to do 
a crossover with Sket Dance,

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.830
since the anime started at 
the same time as ours.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.440
Really, Gin-san?

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.360
They're finally letting us do that too?

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:09.040
I figured that Jump and TV 
Tokyo hated our guts by now.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.860
Since we keep causing problems.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.020
But now I'm nervous,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.090
since I'm actually a pretty shy guy.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.500
What is there to be scared about?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.120
We've done plenty of crossovers.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.240
Have you forgotten when 
we shared the screen

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.830
with Dragonball, One Piece, 
Bleach, and other classics?

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.780
Uh, those were just parodies 
we did without permission.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.630
That would be one of the reasons 
I figured that everybody hated us.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.790
Hey, don't get too excited.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.530
This might be a crossover,

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.450
but our goal isn't to 
have a happy pow-wow.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:36.220
Huh?

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.800
Check out the data I've collected.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.800
Pay attention now.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.630
Sket Dance is a comedy 
manga with a school setting

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.160
that began running in Jump in 2007.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.140
The anime began airing in 2011 at the 
same time the new Gintama began airing.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.110
The Sket Dan is a school club that 
does odd jobs with three members:

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.210
The leader, Bossun.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.140
The brains, Switch.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:59.410
The straight man/muscle, Himeko.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.910
The manga's pretty episodic with 
plenty of laughter and tears.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.970
Hold on, Gin-chan!

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.380
Look at their time slot!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:08.670
It's 6:00 PM on Thursday!

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.040
Huh? Isn't that the old Gintama slot?!

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.460
Exactly.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:19.110
In 2006, after it only took six months 
for us to be booted from prime time,

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.180
we spent the next 177 episodes 
defending that fortress,

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.610
and they just snatched it away from us.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.820
Snatched it away from us?

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.310
It wasn't their decision.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.070
There were obviously extenuating 
circumstances involved.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.840
Well, as I'm sure you can see even 
from my vague explanation,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.150
these guys...

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.990
...are clearly trying to supplant us!

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.410
Uh, why are you trying to twist 
everything before the crossover's even started?

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.060
Clearly trying to overtake us!

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.370
Why are you repeating yourself?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.040
Don't make false accusations.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.170
It's pretty common to find a story 
about people doing odd jobs.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.410
And there are lots of examples 
of series with a trio.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.340
Like this.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.030
And this.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.900
They're all the same.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.140
Uh, did you really 
need to bring that up?

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.320
Yeah, that's right.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.900
It's not the same.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.560
After all, one of them 
uses a computer to talk.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.930
Their characters have more personality.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:08.360
Compared to that, just look at you, Shinpachi.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.110
Why do you talk normally?

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.390
You want me to kill you?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:16.280
Kagura, why haven't you learned any 
genuine Kansai-style witty retorts?

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.730
Why haven't your boobs 
gotten any bigger?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.430
Why are they shrinking?

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:22.330
What was that?!

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.580
You're the one who started 
off wearing goggles

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.150
before they disappeared for no reason!

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.090
Why don't you learn how to Connect?!

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.960
Why don't you get yourself 
a twin brother?!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:31.880
Shut up!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.310
I'm not gonna wear those 
things around every episode!

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.470
Don't you realize the limitations 
of the author's drawing ability?!

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.760
That's why the goggles were removed 
from the beginning of the anime!

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:43.130
You should be grateful you even get any 
screen time in the opening sequences,

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.220
you worthless goggles!

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.110
Uh, are you talking to your goggles?

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.440
Besides, in Jump, 
characters with goggles

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.740
are sidekicks like Usopp 
and kid Konohamaru!

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:56.240
Er, Naruto was wearing 
goggles in volume 1.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.410
And compared to the One Piece 
x Toriko crossover last spring,

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.980
Gintama and Sket Dance 
just lacks pizazz.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.150
It's a boring crossover.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.260
That's not true!

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.750
And don't blame them!

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.180
Why did Jump bother with 
this boring crossover?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.250
I guarantee that they're not 
trying to get us all buddy-buddy.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.830
Then what's the point of this crossover?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.660
That should be obvious.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.630
Wh-Who is it?!

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.960
You don't need two Jump shows

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.220
about people doing odd jobs 
at 6 PM on TV Tokyo.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.470
They're pitting us against one another 
because of our similar settings.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.900
To see whether the Sket Dan or you guys 
are more worthy as Jump's odd jobbers!

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.900
Bastards!

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.830
I think it's amusing.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.190
Let's go along with 
Jump's little scheme.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.660
We had to settle this sooner or later.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.920
Stop that, Bossun. Show some respect.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.910
They've been in Jump 
longer than we have.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.230
Sorry about that. He 
usually isn't so rude.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.900
He's a nice boy deep down.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.080
Stop acting like my mom!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.550
Bossun, that should be, 
"Stop acting like my ma!"

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.980
You rock, Switch!

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.680
You already know how 
to fit in this world!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.050
I mean, ya already know 
how to fit in this world!

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:10.000
Don't just barge in here 
and start making fun of us!

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:10.810
Pisses me off!

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.940
You're destroying our characters!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.020
You're clearly set on crushing us!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.880
Hey, Himeko. Have they really 
been around longer than us?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.210
They seem really worried.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:23.110
Bossun, that's the secret 
to their success.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.290
They've spent years pretending 
to be the weak link

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.460
so they can bash other series 
without any repercussions.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.310
Stop spilling the beans, 
four-eyed computer boy!

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.080
Want me to nail down your enter key?!

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.410
Spilling the beans?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:37.100
Why are you talking to yourself 
anyway? The hell is this?

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:41.630
What was that?! You wanna know how 
it feels to talk to yourself?!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.100
Shinpachi, let him have it!

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.340
What? Me?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.350
Fine then.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:47.850
H-Hold on...

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.640
Recite the 12th clause of the 
Tsuu Terakado Fanclub creed!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.950
Taka-chin!

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:56.110
E-Er, I'm not Taka-chin.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.580
You can't fool me, 
your childhood friend.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.620
I mean, look.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:00.680
What's up, Shin-chan?

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:01.870
I'm Taka-chin.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.350
You can't fool me!

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.690
Then I'll send in Teppei.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.600
Bossun, where are we?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.200
This makes it harder for me!

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.390
Now, now. Stop fighting.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.540
Okay, Runny Diarrhea.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.550
R-Runny...

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.110
Teach, Bossun-kun and Pachi-boy-kun 
made Himeko-san cry!

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.220
I'm not crying!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.860
D-Does this mean...

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.280
It can't mean that...

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.720
I was cast as...

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.940
Jugem Jugem Shit-Tossing the Life of

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.000
Shin-chan's Two-Day-Old Underwear

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.190
Balmung Fezalion Issac Schneider

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:39.440
1/3 True Love 2/3 Hangnail Anxiety

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:42.870
Betrayal Knows My Name Or Does It Really

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.360
Ignore Calls Squid Dogfish 
Halibut Trout-Cod Dogfish...

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.660
This Is a Different Dogfish,

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.060
I'm Talking About The Dogfish Shark

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:49.510
Kaluga Angler Ray

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.580
Yuuteimiyaoukimukou 
Pepepepepepepepepepepepe

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.480
Runny Diarrhea

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.250
...just for this?!

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.020
Yes, just so we could do that.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.250
That's despicable!

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:04.470
We get in the first word since our 
side of the crossover airs earlier.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.010
Now even in the parts of the manga 
where we parodied other works,

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.030
people will think that 
you're copying us.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.020
Man, Gintama's desperate.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:15.770
I'm kinda creeped out.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.840
They aren't aware that 
in most decisive battles,

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:20.770
the one who attacks first usually loses.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.900
Fine then!

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:28.070
Let's make it clear which team has the 
pizazz to be worthy of Jump.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.640
This is supposed to be a crossover.

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.160
Let's all get along.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:37.070
Hah, we'll show you that flashy battles 
and special attacks aren't everything.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.250
I doubt the viewers are 
going to appreciate this.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.880
Yeah, equally boring anime 
shows should get along.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.340
We should be glad that 
we're still on air.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.440
Shut up! This isn't just about our position.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.020
Our pride as odd-jobbing Jumpers, 
and our very existence, is on the line!

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.660
You mob characters should just 
shut up and follow your leader!

00:08:58.660 --> 00:08:59.730
That's right!

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.020
C'mon down! I got everything set up!

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.500
<b>Impact</b>

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:21.920
<b>Amethystyx (Pachimon type) Capture Level -26</b>

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.430
Gin-chan, where are we?

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.450
The Gintama world was already a stretch,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.680
and now we're in a place 
that's even weirder, Bossun.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:32.530
Okay, quiet down.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.180
Listen up.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:38.460
We're going to have a little 
scavenger hunt on this island.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.690
Why are you talking like a teacher?

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:47.540
We're on Treasure Island, an island where 
shiny gems grow on everything.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.400
This sounds awfully familiar.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.660
There is a legend that every hundred 
years, the gems bear a very special fruit.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.200
I have a really bad feeling about this.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:01.460
Yes! One of the famous Devil Fruit!

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.440
The Pizazz-Pizazz Fruit!

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.960
Hold it right there!

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.860
This is supposed to be a Sket 
Dance x Gintama crossover!

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.920
But now we're in the Toriko 
x One Piece crossover!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.750
We might be boring, but 
that doesn't make it okay

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.470
to steal ideas from series 
that have more pizazz!

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.530
Toriko and One Piece?

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.740
What are they babbling about?

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.530
You must have had some of 
that Dream-Dream Fruit.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.440
They're starting to piss me off.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.440
Hopeless fools.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:28.980
They must have eaten 
the Argh-Argh Fruit.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.530
As you may have guessed,

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.660
the Pizazz-Pizazz fruit can 
give the dullest people pizazz!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.490
Whoever finds it first,

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:42.000
will be declared the winner of the contest 
with the flashiness worthy of Jump!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.860
I thought we were fighting over who 
had the pizazz worthy of Jump.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.180
But now we've given up?

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:47.460
We're going to rely on outside help?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.410
I have a question.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.330
Does this Devil Fruit 
have any side effects,

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.960
such as turning one 
into a hammer in water?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.390
It's fine. You won't lose 
the ability to swim.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:01.390
I see. So you've changed 
the setting a little.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.140
Only your crotch turns into a hammer.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.470
I see, that's good.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.390
Huh?

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.650
What did you just say?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.630
Well, it's only your crotch 
that turns into a hammer,

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.270
so you don't need to worry.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.970
I'm worried!

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:18.410
Why is there a hammer down there?!

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.240
Stop that, seriously.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.550
We're supposed to be innocent, 
unlike you people.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.810
We don't do dirty jokes!

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.960
Himeko-san, I'll handle this.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.920
As the straight man, I'm used 
to this, so leave it to me!

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:34.380
The hammer's upside down!

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:36.200
It should be like this!

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.800
Who cares?!

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.890
Aren't you supposed to be 
the Gintama straight man?!

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.540
Why are you acting like the funny man?!

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:45.900
I'm not going to last long if I 
have to respond to both sides!

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.190
I'm sorry, I thought I 
could let you handle it.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.580
Right. So who cares if 
it's upside down or not.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.610
If I have a hammer on my 
crotch, I can't get married.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:54.830
Are you going to take responsibility?

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:55.820
Isn't that right, Kagura-chan?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.010
Why? What's the problem?

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:03.020
A hammer makes a better 
weapon than a hockey stick.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.330
I asked the wrong person!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.000
No, no! Think this through!

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.850
You can't survive in this wacky manga

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:10.340
when you have a hammer on your crotch!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:12.090
You don't need to worry.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:16.640
If you grow a hammer down there, 
Bossun will boss into a nail for you.

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:17.320
What the hell?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.020
What's that mean?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.350
Why would I boss into a nail?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.120
Hey, bitch. Enough already.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.390
Did you call me a bitch?!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.730
You aren't in your puny 
little school anymore.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.170
In this world, your crotch 
can grow into a screwdriver

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:33.110
or your balls can get 
crushed at any time.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:33.940
What kind of world is this?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:35.700
If you want to do odd jobs,

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.620
you gotta be ready for your 
crotch to do odd jobs.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.950
That's not how it's supposed to work!

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.200
Oh, really?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.130
You're picking a fight with us when you 
aren't ready to get down and dirty?

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:49.250
You shouldn't be so happy just because 
AKB did your theme song.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.910
It's not AKB anymore!

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:51.800
Are you jealous?

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.490
Say that you're jealous that we got AKB!

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.210
Your token glasses character 
must be jealous!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.260
Not really!

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.260
Fine then!

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:02.930
I'll be the one to turn 
my crotch into a hammer!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.270
Uh, wrong objective, Bossun!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:08.190
No good. Bossun has lost his head.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:11.730
Your leader doesn't like to lose either.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.770
I want nothing to do with this.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:16.530
Don't come to me when you lose viewers 
because your crotch is a hammer.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.830
We'll just have to stand by and watch.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.150
Bossun has always had a complex

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:23.530
about how he's too boring 
to be a main character.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.370
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:28.860
Gin-san always complains about how 
he should have a special attack.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:32.000
That's why it's so hard to make games.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.920
That's why Bandai Namco gave up on us.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.210
Oh, we're going to have that problem.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.120
There's always Hyperion and Genesis.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.050
Those are crap.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.760
We need something like Bankai or Stands.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.210
Oh, I've seen Gin-chan 
secretly practicing

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:50.160
his Kamehameha two or three times.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:52.190
Ouch. Just ouch.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:57.440
Right. Bossun has that Connecting 
special power when he wears his goggles.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:01.550
But really, it just looks 
like he put on his goggles.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.160
Does he yell, "Goggles on!"

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.300
He did at first.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.990
Kind of like how your guy 
wore goggles at first.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.130
They should stick to it.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:13.500
To be honest, I don't think 
it's about special attacks.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:16.840
Between his silver hair and that hat, 
he's tried a lot of things to stand out,

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.590
but people with pizazz 
just have it already.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.550
Yeah.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:23.050
You can't be a main character 
when you complain to your buddies

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.490
about not standing out.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.280
Luffy would never say 
anything like that.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.640
You're never going to hear him say, "I 
will become a main character with pizazz!"

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.690
Yeah?

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:34.190
That's why these guys just fail.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:37.780
If they're going to bother competing, 
they should set their sights higher.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:40.680
Really, does it matter who wins?

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.490
They're in the same boat anyway.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:45.950
Indeed, their weak will is 
embodied by their weak goals.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:50.690
They don't have any goals like becoming 
the Pirate King or becoming the Hokage.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:52.650
I'm getting worried about 
throwing my lot in with him.

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:54.460
He's too wishy-washy.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:59.560
I should have gone with a reliable 
main character like Luffy.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.290
I want Aya Tojo!

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.560
I prefer Nishino.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.250
I prefer Raoh!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.720
Uh, none of those are main characters.

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:12.600
Huh? They disappeared.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.610
Oh, they fell down.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:23.560
Hey, are you okay? Gin-san? Bo-san?

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.000
I'm already...

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:27.980
...sick of this.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.120
They said something. 
But I can't hear them.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:32.940
I'm already...

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.120
...sick of this.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:38.380
They're the ones who 
ran off by themselves.

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.270
What? You're giving up on 
finding the Devil Fruit?

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.280
Let's go home then.

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:47.080
We need to wrap up this episode.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.780
They really want attention.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.640
They're the ones who dragged us into this... 
what are they trying to do?

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.750
Just ignore them and go back.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:57.600
I agree.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.200
I must return to my enjoyment 
of To Love-Ru Darkness.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.980
Uh, Himeko-san.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.290
Sorry about the Runny Diarrhea thing.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:06.690
Nah, it's okay.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.740
This crossover was new and fun.

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.330
Like...

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:17.670
Like, you guys don't 
understand how we feel.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.670
Uh oh, he's going to 
start monologuing again.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.590
It's not that we want pizazz, 
or that we want to stand out.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.080
That's not what drives us.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.640
We're doing this for 
the sake of our teams,

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.440
but none of you even care.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.730
Yeah, yeah. Forget it.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.150
There's no point in trying 
to explain to them.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.140
Wait, I'm really upset about this.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.910
Don't you feel the same way, Sakata-san?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.150
He just called him Sakata-san.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.580
Forget it. Just forget it.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:47.870
Stop talking.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.280
I know how you feel.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.920
It's not easy being the leader.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.020
They're buddies now.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:55.920
Uh, sorry.

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:57.800
Could you leave?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:02.580
Feel free to go join Luffy or Raoh or whoever.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.090
We leaders are going to 
do this by ourselves.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:08.490
This is bad. They heard 
what we were saying.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.130
Hey. Pull yourself together, Bossun.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.300
Can you stand?

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.060
Uh, Gin-san. We're sorry.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.770
You've got it wrong! You've 
got it wrong, Bossun!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.220
We were just joking!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:20.710
We just wanted to give 
you a little push.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:24.410
It's not like you need 
to apologize or anything.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.460
Everything you said 
was absolutely right.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:33.510
An apology won't heal Bossun 
and Gin-san's wounded hearts!

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.760
What's going on?

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:37.700
I can't tell if they want 
us to apologize or not.

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.520
They left. Should we just ignore them?

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.440
They got mad when we tried to apologize.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:45.110
Those leaders are too hard to deal with.

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.810
How naive can they be?

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.390
Hmm? They're not moving forward.

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:54.590
They're walking in place.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.620
They're waiting for us to say something.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.580
What a pain!

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:58.920
What are they trying to do?!

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.930
Hang in there!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.100
Now they're acting.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.980
Where did Bossun injure 
himself?! His head?!

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:06.830
Hey, this isn't good.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.160
They're not chasing after us.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:09.440
They've given up on us.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.380
Why?! Aren't they worried about me?

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.990
They don't care about their leader?!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:16.940
At this rate, we'll lose 
our status as leaders.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:21.500
We have to find the Pizazz-Pizazz 
Fruit to regain their trust.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.980
H-Hey, look there!

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.780
There it is!

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.010
What? They just took off.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:34.300
Did they find the Devil Fruit?

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:35.950
Pathetic.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:38.090
They've revealed their true 
colors and started to fight.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:43.150
Let go! I'm going to get pizazz!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.690
I'll become a brutal 
genius with an IQ of 300

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:48.400
whose hair turns silver 
when my powers awaken!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.490
Over my dead body!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.180
The pizazz is mine!

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:52.950
I'll become a space pirate 
who's lost his memories with

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:54.520
a Psycho-gun on my right arm and

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.200
travel around space with hot women!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.560
Almost there!

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:02.730
So close to the pizazz!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.350
Who is that guy?

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:07.420
That's a dangerous place to stand.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.500
Honey, forgive me for going on ahead.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.430
I can't do any carpentry 
when my hand's like this.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.920
Can't even hold a hammer...

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:18.930
Damn it.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.430
But I'm healthy down there.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:25.050
If my crotch became a hammer,

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:27.910
I could use my rapid hip 
movements to hammer nails.

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:31.650
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.670
Hold on, gramps!

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.410
Gramps! Your request...

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:44.300
...has been accepted!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:29.570
So in the end, neither 
of them got any pizazz.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:33.150
But there's nothing 
wrong with being boring.

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.920
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:40.190
They're great odd jobbers.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.540
They're great leaders.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.570
Hey, why are you so blue?

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:48.140
Cheer up, guys.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.940
You looked good back 
there. I'm impressed.

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:53.750
Let's call this a draw.

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:55.010
Next time, we won't lose.

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:56.430
Fine by me.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:58.990
Next time, we'll wreck you!

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:01.440
To finish, you twist the story into 
something resembling a good ending.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:02.790
That's as Gintama as you get.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.090
Exactly.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.370
This way, you have a 
sense of completion.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.880
Uh, can you stop that?

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:16.380
The episode's over.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:18.390
Were you really that 
desperate for some pizazz?

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.510
It's okay.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.450
No, that's not it...

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:26.780
When we threw the Pizazz-Pizazz 
Fruit at the old man,

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.520
some of the juice sprayed out.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:48.400
Everyone, tune in next 
week for Carpenter Dance

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.410
and Gin-Balls.

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.510
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:37.520
<b>Notice: This footage isn't real.</b>

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:27.050
Next time on Gintama,

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:29.820
Odd Jobs suddenly appears 
in the Sket Dan clubroom.

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:31.380
Wait, isn't this the preview 
for our episode this week?!

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:33.210
Why are you showing a 
preview for our show?!

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:34.450
And why are you showing fake footage?!

00:23:34.450 --> 00:23:36.520
Well, it just happened as I was 
following the original.

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:37.520
What's that mean?!

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:38.260
Is this really okay?

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.530
<b>Episode 26</b>

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:40.030
Next time: Spirit Dance!

00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:42.170
We're the academy support group!

00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:43.680
Carpenter Dance!
